---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: Authentication | Shellui
description: Sign-in lives in the Shellui shell. identity-service (Django) runs OAuth with GitHub, Google, or Microsoft, issues JWTs, and publishes a JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) so other services can verify them. Supabase Auth is the swap.
eyebrow: Features
heading: Authentication in the shell
lede: The shell owns /login so your iframe app does not ship a login page. It stores the session and shares the signed-in user over the SDK. The default backend is identity-service, a Django API; set backend.type to supabase if Auth is already in your stack.
pageScripts:
  - /assets/js/auth-flow.js
---

<section aria-labelledby="auth-exchange">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="auth-exchange" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">How the iframe, shell, and identity-service talk</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">OAuth must run in the top window, so an embedded app calls <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.login()</code> and the shell starts identity-service authorize. identity-service talks to the provider, confirms the account, then redirects to <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">/login/callback</code> with tokens in the URL fragment.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "auth-flow.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="identity-service-does">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="identity-service-does" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">What identity-service does</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">identity-service is a Django backend for <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">backend.type: "shellui"</code>. It exposes a Shellui-compatible auth API at <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">/api/v1/*</code>. Source lives in the <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 dark:text-primary" href="{{ site.identityService }}">identity-service</a> repo.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">OAuth providers</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">GitHub, Google, and Microsoft. Per-company OAuth clients. A sign-in method picker, even when only one provider is enabled, then an account confirmation screen.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">JWT and JWKS</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Access and refresh tokens are RS256 JWTs. Other services verify them with a JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) at <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">GET /.well-known/jwks.json</code> when <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">JWT_PRIVATE_KEY</code> is set. Refresh with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">grant_type=refresh_token</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Company join modes</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">After a successful provider login, access is per company: public, a domain allow list, or invitation only. The same account can be enabled in one tenant and waiting in another.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Redirect allowlist</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Provider apps register one callback on identity-service. The shell origin must be allowlisted so identity-service can redirect tokens in the URL fragment. Loopback is always allowed so <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">shellui login</code> works.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Directory APIs</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Staff and owners list users, enable membership, patch company access, and manage OAuth clients. Group names travel on the JWT as <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">user.groups</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Other login methods</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">The shell login page can show <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">magic_link</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">web3</code>, or <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">password</code> when the backend advertises them. Email magic link is the Supabase path today. identity-service ships OAuth first.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="connect-and-guard">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="connect-and-guard" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Connect a backend and guard routes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">backend</code> in config. Mark navigation with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">requiresAuth</code>. Signed-out visitors go to login, then back to the page they asked for.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink dark:text-primary">1. Connect a backend</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">backend</code> in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">shellui.config.json</code> and enable the login methods you want on the page.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink dark:text-primary">2. Protect routes</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Mark navigation with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">requiresAuth</code>. The iframe URL does not load until you sign in.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink dark:text-primary">3. Login from the iframe</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">From an embedded app, call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">shellui.login()</code> so the shell can start the redirect.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "ts", "shellui.config.ts" %}
import type { ShellUIConfig } from "@shellui/core";

const config: ShellUIConfig = {
  backend: {
    type: "shellui",
    url: "http://localhost:8000",
    companyId: 1,
    login: {
      methods: ["oauth"],
      oauthProviders: ["github", "google"],
    },
  },
  navigation: [
    {
      label: "Billing",
      path: "billing",
      url: "https://app.example.com/billing",
      requiresAuth: true,
    },
  ],
};

export default config;
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
</section>

